## 3. Codebase Analysis & Strategic Guidance

The following analysis is based on my direct review of the current codebase. Use these notes and tips to guide your implementation.

### Relevant Existing Code
*   **File:** `modules/core-platform/src/main/java/villagecompute/storefront/api/rest/StorefrontResource.java`
    *   **Summary:** Qute-backed storefront controller that renders `/`, `/product/:slug`, `/cart`, `/checkout`, and account routes. It relies on `CatalogService` for catalog data, `LocalizationService` for message bundles, and inlined helpers to parse `Accept-Language`, build language options, and hydrate theme token maps from generated JSON under `templates/storefront/_generated`. Tenant context (`TenantContext`) is read at the start of each handler, and template data dictionaries (hero, featured products, cart, etc.) are assembled before rendering `Templates.index()`.
    *   **Recommendation:** Introduce the planned `ThemeProvider` CDI bean and inject it here so `buildThemeTokens` becomes reusable + cacheable rather than a private helper; centralize JSON loading + fallback logic there. When adding the Accept-Language preference cookie, reuse the existing `resolveLocale` helper and extend endpoints that need to set cookies to return `Response` objects so you can attach a `NewCookie` without breaking template rendering. Keep using `mapProductsToDisplayData` so the product grid stays consistent with other pages.
*   **File:** `modules/core-platform/src/main/java/villagecompute/storefront/api/rest/ProductResource.java`
    *   **Summary:** REST API exposing `/api/v1/catalog/products` and related variant endpoints. It enforces tenant scope via `TenantContext`, delegates to `CatalogService`, emits Micrometer metrics, and maps entities to DTOs via `ProductMapper` before returning paginated JSON.
    *   **Recommendation:** Use this resource (or the injected `CatalogService` it wraps) as the authoritative data source for the sample product grid. Align any new DTOs with `ProductSummary` so storefront templates and REST responses stay in sync, and keep respecting feature flags like `catalog.search.enabled` when deciding which data to surface.
*   **File:** `modules/core-platform/src/main/resources/templates/base.html`
    *   **Summary:** Global Qute layout used by storefront pages. It sets up the `<head>` metadata, injects tenant CSS variables via `storefront/_theme.css`, includes Tailwind/PrimeUI assets, renders the header/footer includes, and defines slots for page-specific content and scripts.
    *   **Recommendation:** When wiring multi-tenant theming, continue to pass a `themeTokens` map into this template so the inline `<style>` block can apply CSS custom properties. Any new Accept-Language cookie UI hints (e.g., showing the active locale) should remain in components pulled into this layout, not inlined per-page.
*   **File:** `modules/core-platform/src/main/resources/templates/StorefrontResource/index.html`
    *   **Summary:** Home page template that extends `base.html`, renders hero content, category rail, featured products, and optional collections by iterating over `featuredProducts`, `rootCategories`, and `collections` data supplied by `StorefrontResource`.
    *   **Recommendation:** Populate the data maps expected here (heroData, rootCategories, featuredProducts, etc.) when implementing the theme provider + product grid requirements. Keep the structure and CSS utility classes aligned with Tailwind tokens so future theming remains token-driven.
*   **File:** `modules/core-platform/src/main/resources/templates/components/product-card.html`
    *   **Summary:** Reusable product tile used on the homepage grid. It expects fields like `product.slug`, `imageUrl`, `price`, `compareAtPrice`, `onSale`, and `averageRating`, and already uses `{msg:*}` keys for localization.
    *   **Recommendation:** Ensure whatever DTO feeds featured products includes the fields this component consumes (especially `price`, `compareAtPrice`, `categoryName`, `onSale`, `inStock`). If you introduce theme-driven color classes, prefer leveraging CSS variables defined in `_theme.css` so this component automatically reflects tenant branding.

### Implementation Tips & Notes
*   **Tip:** `modules/core-platform/src/main/resources/templates/storefront/_theme.css` is already wired into `base.html`; have your new `ThemeProvider` return a flat `Map<String,String>` keyed like `primary500`, `secondary600`, etc., so the partial continues to resolve `{themeTokens.primary500}` without refactoring.
*   **Tip:** `LocalizationService` (`modules/core-platform/src/main/java/villagecompute/storefront/util/LocalizationService.java`) loads message bundles from `modules/core-platform/src/main/resources/messages/`. Reuse it when persisting the visitor’s locale preference—resolve the locale the same way everywhere, then set a cookie (e.g., `lang`) that `resolveLocale` can check before consulting `Accept-Language`.
*   **Tip:** Place new storefront-facing tests alongside `modules/core-platform/src/test/java/villagecompute/storefront/api/rest/StorefrontResourceUnitTest.java`. Follow that pattern (reflection helpers + CDI injection mocking) for any `ThemeProviderTest`, and seed `TenantContext` in tests before touching services that expect it.
*   **Note:** Actual source paths live under `modules/core-platform/...` rather than the generic `src/...` paths mentioned in the plan. Keep that in mind when creating new Java classes or Qute templates so Quarkus picks them up without extra build wiring.
*   **Warning:** Theme data currently comes from generated JSON files referenced by `THEME_RESOURCE_PREFIX`. When you add caching, make sure invalidation hooks respond to future CDI events (e.g., `TenantThemeUpdated`) and continue to fall back to the `default` entry so requests for tenants without custom themes don’t 500. Also ensure every request still reads `TenantContext` before loading theme data to avoid cross-tenant leakage.
EOF
